,"lo":5,"hi":11,"source":"snpp_scaled","aqua":4,"snpp":30,"noaa20":32,"flags":[],"median_ref":8.0,"anomaly_pct":0.0}],"note":"Real. NASA FIRMS MODIS C6.1 and VIIRS daily counts (yearly country archives), 2-degree cell -98 to -96 E, 38 to 40 N. Exploratory: same method as the presets, not checked against a national reference series. aqua, snpp, noaa20 = raw monthly counts of all daytime detections. fixed = Aqua count before 2012 (Aqua's clock had not drifted), then S-NPP count x the 2012-2020 Aqua/S-NPP ratio for that calendar month, in Aqua units (a VIIRS-based Aqua-equivalent estimate). lo/hi = uncertainty in the historical conversion ratio only, null for observed Aqua months; it omits outage filling and changes in relative detectability. source = aqua_observed, snpp_scaled or snpp_scaled_noaa20_filled. Full calendar months, not the audit's matched days. S-NPP outage days filled with NOAA-20 x 1.040. outage flag = 3 or more S-NPP outage days in the month. median_ref = median fixed count for that calendar month, 2002-2025."}